{"w":2400,"h":3396,"lines":[{"y":0.032634577269658127,"c":1,"w":0.083171049753824944,"h":0.015594571161888005,"t":"Reading","x":0.83510980490622233},{"y":0.079506088294647004,"x":0.32488625952787875,"t":"The Step Pyramid of Djoser","w":0.34813585917154943,"h":0.022409380675766255,"c":1},{"h":0.017445284570484998,"w":0.72839508056640623,"x":0.12345678054441464,"y":0.1191860463510136,"c":1,"t":"The pyramids are the most famous monuments of ancient Egypt and still hold"},{"w":0.77366256713867188,"h":0.017441860778592999,"c":1,"x":0.12551439531990469,"y":0.13808139518837192,"t":"enormous interest for people in the present day. These grand, impressive tributes to"},{"w":0.79043334960937495,"y":0.1542241656772223,"c":1,"h":0.024268212110611476,"x":0.12534459347742094,"t":"the memory of the Egyptian kings have become linked with the country even though"},{"x":0.12551441560006349,"t":"other cultures, such as the Chinese and Mayan, also built pyramids. The evolution of","w":0.79218104044596349,"h":0.018972387864255591,"c":1,"y":0.17579505341541024},{"y":0.19611307443736281,"c":1,"t":"the pyramid form has been written and argued about for centuries. However, there","w":0.76543207804361979,"h":0.019140164899882239,"x":0.12551441354639623},{"t":"is no question that, as far as Egypt is concerned, it began with one monument to one","w":0.78806584676106761,"h":0.018963828384525261,"x":0.12345678845230064,"y":0.21366279107520558,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.12551439992250552,"t":"king designed by one brilliant architect: the Step Pyramid of Djoser at Saqgara.","y":0.23401162774468376,"w":0.74279836018880196,"h":0.017460692757290786},{"x":0.12345678782340978,"y":0.26295641948409321,"t":"Djoser was the first king of the Third Dynasty of Egypt and the first to build in","w":0.7366255187988282,"c":1,"h":0.017667844522968212},{"w":0.79218104044596349,"t":"stone. Prior to Djoser's reign, tombs were rectangular monuments made of dried clay","h":0.01896554028047126,"x":0.12551441406199776,"c":1,"y":0.2819767443417005},{"x":0.12551441166530508,"w":0.77777776082356787,"y":0.30232558123627862,"t":"brick, which covered underground passages where the deceased person was buried.","h":0.017462404653237007,"c":1},{"y":0.31837863768628072,"t":"For reasons which remain unclear, Djoser's main official, whose name was Imhotep,","w":0.78621475219726578,"h":0.021776372327680926,"c":1,"x":0.12541996919789114},{"w":0.77366251627604166,"y":0.33863368642290115,"h":0.018924452531183245,"t":"conceived of building a taller, more impressive tomb for his king by stacking stone","x":0.12551442128584747,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.76748972574869789,"x":0.12345678311372704,"y":0.35895170744367333,"t":"slabs on top of one another, progressively making them smaller, to form the shape","h":0.018955268904794931},{"y":0.37433282671141077,"t":"now known as the Step Pyramid. Djoser is thought to have reigned for 19 years, but","x":0.12335769446504609,"w":0.78418502807617185,"h":0.024180687498849718,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"some historians and scholars attribute a much longer time for his rule, owing to the","w":0.77777776082356775,"y":0.39811542988837934,"x":0.12345679849369863,"h":0.019140164899882239},{"h":0.014534883982160629,"c":1,"w":0.41152262369791665,"x":0.12551440821946641,"t":"number and size of the monuments he built.","y":0.41715116265578223},{"x":0.12551439847793272,"h":0.017667844522968212,"w":0.69753087361653643,"y":0.44611307445048132,"t":"The Step Pyramid has been thoroughly examined and investigated over the","c":1},{"w":0.730452677408854,"t":"last century, and it is now known that the building process went through many","h":0.01751034054795475,"c":1,"x":0.12345678878118567,"y":0.46511627890962248},{"y":0.48255813934786951,"h":0.020386501532421053,"t":"different stages. Historian Marc Van de Mieroop comments on this, writing 'Much","x":0.12551439631310377,"w":0.76748972574869789,"c":1},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"w":0.75720163981119792,"c":1,"y":0.50290697658404115,"t":"experimentation was involved, which is especially clear in the construction of the","x":0.12551440636111921},{"x":0.12541099963178945,"w":0.76149403889973954,"t":"pyramid in the center of the complex. It had several plans... before it became the","h":0.021007691732705447,"c":1,"y":0.51972690886138628},{"t":"first Step Pyramid in history, piling six levels on top of one another ... The weight","x":0.12551439630296671,"h":0.01895698080074093,"y":0.54063604205991223,"w":0.76748972574869789,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"of the enormous mass was a challenge for the builders, who placed the stones at an","x":0.12551439531692021,"w":0.77366256713867188,"y":0.56095406347068866,"h":0.017667844522968212},{"h":0.020380244799862224,"c":1,"y":0.57845688918526872,"x":0.12338994421422096,"t":"inward incline in order to prevent the monument breaking up?","w":0.58452540079752602},{"c":1,"h":0.017501780506578801,"x":0.12551440538359068,"w":0.76337448120117191,"y":0.60895170801979592,"t":"When finally completed, the Step Pyramid rose 62 meters high and was the tallest"},{"t":"structure of its time. The complex in which it was built was the size of a city in","x":0.12551440100613273,"y":0.6277974085042739,"w":0.73662551879882798,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"t":"ancient Egypt and included a temple, courtyards, shrines, and living quarters for the","x":0.12345678026279558,"h":0.018980948467277048,"y":0.64680232596989096,"w":0.78600824991861984,"c":1},{"y":0.66569767425314541,"t":"priests. It covered a region of 16 hectares and was surrounded by a wall 10.5 meters","w":0.78189300537109374,"h":0.017458980861344786,"x":0.12551440229181934,"c":1},{"t":"high. The wall had 13 false doors cut into it with only one true entrance cut into the","w":0.77993555704752604,"c":1,"x":0.12546011847169022,"y":0.68443536437526742,"h":0.018630993801516782},{"w":0.76748967488606779,"x":0.1234568091207521,"y":0.70347467600505575,"h":0.018909044344377457,"c":1,"t":"south-east corner; the entire wall was then ringed by a trench 750 meters long and"},{"c":1,"w":0.77366256713867188,"h":0.017486372881418633,"x":0.12551439531560124,"y":0.72379269703987381,"t":"40 meters wide. The false doors and the trench were incorporated into the complex"},{"h":0.018989507947007378,"t":"to discourage unwanted visitors. If someone wished to enter, he or she would have","x":0.12345679943838206,"y":0.74263839863513648,"w":0.77160491943359377,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.77366256713867188,"x":0.12551439660899044,"y":0.76017441895150817,"t":"needed to know in advance how to find the location of the true opening in the wall.","h":0.018977524675384938},{"t":"Djoser was so proud of his accomplishment that he broke the tradition of having","y":0.7805232560008375,"x":0.12551440379864742,"h":0.017474388486504955,"c":1,"w":0.75102879842122394},{"t":"only his own name on the monument and had Imhotep's name carved on it as well.","x":0.1254619972472463,"y":0.79923493580219185,"h":0.019156555966578281,"c":1,"w":0.77169779459635435},{"y":0.90552325564189406,"x":0.8909465021607732,"w":0.024691357612609877,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"21"}]}